{"book":10,"chapter":6,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / GETTING TO KNOW RUST / CHAPTER 6","slides":[{"title":"Two strings","sub":"Chapter 6 · &str and String","short":"Intro","main":"&str to read, String to own and change.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Two strings","&str","String"],"captions":["Python has one immutable string; Rust has two types: &str and String","&str is a reference to text: we read it but do not own it","String is owned by the program: it can grow and change"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Python: str","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Rust: &str, String","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":200.0,"h":40.0,"text":"&str: look","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":200.0,"h":40.0,"text":"String: own","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[11.1,27.6]}]},{"title":"Literals","sub":"&'static str","short":"Literals","main":"A literal is baked into the program and never changes; raw strings r\"…\".","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Literal","Raw strings","Multi-line"],"captions":["\"text\" has type &'static str: it lives in the program itself and never changes","r\"C:\\dir\" and r#\"…\"…\"## are raw strings, nothing is escaped","A backslash at the end of a line continues the literal on the next line"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let s: &str = \"hello\";","// read-only"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let p = r\"C:\\Users\\bob\";","let q = r#\"he said \"yes\"\"#;"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let s = \"first \\","    second\";","// \"first second\""],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.0,22.8]}]},{"title":"String","sub":"Creating and growing","short":"String","main":"String::from, to_string, new; push and push_str; bytes on the heap.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Creating","push and push_str","Heap and capacity"],"captions":["String::from(\"…\"), \"…\".to_string(), String::new() — three ways","let mut s = String::new(); s.push('a'); s.push_str(\"bc\"); — appending","On the stack: pointer, length, capacity; the bytes live on the heap and grow as needed"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let a = String::from(\"rust\");","let b = \"rust\".to_string();","let c = String::new();"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let mut s = String::new();","s.push('a');","s.push_str(\"bc\");   // \"abc\""],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":80.0,"y":40.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"ptr →","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":80.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"len = 6","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":80.0,"y":100.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"cap = 8","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"h","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":120.0,"h":80.0,"text":"bytes on the heap","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.9,25.4]}]},{"title":"Concatenation","sub":"+, format!, join","short":"Concatenation","main":"+ takes the left string; format! and join take nothing.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["+","format!","join"],"captions":["s1 + &s2: String on the left, &str on the right; s1 is unusable afterwards — + consumes the left string","format!(\"{} {}\", a, b) takes nothing and works like an f-string","[\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"].join(\", \") — joins a list with a separator"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let s1 = String::from(\"ab\");","let s2 = String::from(\"cd\");","let s3 = s1 + &s2;   // s1 is moved"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let name = \"Anya\";","let t = format!(\"Hello, {name}!\");"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let v = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"];","let s = v.join(\", \");   // \"a, b, c\""],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[9.5,29.4]}]},{"title":"UTF-8","sub":"Bytes and characters","short":"UTF-8","main":"len is bytes, chars().count() is characters.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Bytes per character","len() ≠ characters","chars().count()"],"captions":["UTF-8: Latin is 1 byte, Cyrillic 2, CJK 3, emoji 4","\"привет\".len() = 12: len counts bytes, not characters","\"привет\".chars().count() = 6 — the number of characters"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"a — 1","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"\"я\" — 2","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"世 — 3","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"😀 — 4","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":220.0,"h":28.0,"text":"\"п р и в е т\"","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"text":"6 characters × 2 = 12 bytes","size":11.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let s = \"привет\";","s.len()            // 12","s.chars().count() // 6"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":22.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[13.0,24.7]}]},{"title":"Indexing and slices","sub":"Character boundaries","short":"Slices","main":"s[0] is not allowed; slice at boundaries; get and nth.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["No indexing","Byte slice","get"],"captions":["s[0] does not compile: a character may take several bytes","&s[0..4] is the first two Cyrillic letters; a boundary mid-character panics","s.get(0..3) returns None instead of panicking; the n-th character is s.chars().nth(n)"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let s = \"привет\";","let c = s[0];   // ✕"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["&s[0..4]   // \"пр\"","&s[0..3]   // panic: not a boundary"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["s.get(0..3)         // None","s.chars().nth(2)    // Some('и')"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[14.3,32.5]}]},{"title":"Iteration","sub":"chars, split, lines","short":"Iteration","main":"chars, bytes, char_indices, split_whitespace, lines, split.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["chars and bytes","split_whitespace and lines","split"],"captions":["chars gives characters, bytes gives bytes, char_indices gives (position, character) pairs","split_whitespace splits on spaces, lines splits into lines","split(',') splits on any separator; collect gathers the result into a Vec"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["for c in s.chars() { }","for b in s.bytes() { }","for (i, c) in s.char_indices() { }"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["for w in text.split_whitespace() { }","for line in text.lines() { }"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let parts: Vec<&str> =","    \"a,b,c\".split(',').collect();"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[11.0,21.9]}]},{"title":"Methods","sub":"contains, replace, trim","short":"Methods","main":"Searches and transformations return a new value.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Search","Transform","New value"],"captions":["contains, starts_with, ends_with, find (position or None)","to_uppercase, to_lowercase, replace, trim","Methods return a new string; the original is unchanged — save the result"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["s.contains(\"ra\")","s.starts_with(\"Ra\")","s.find(\"t\")     // Some(..)"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["s.to_uppercase()","s.replace(\"a\", \"o\")","\"  x  \".trim()   // \"x\""],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let up = s.to_uppercase();","// s is still the same"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[14.4,26.3]}]},{"title":"split and parse","sub":"Parsing text into numbers","short":"Parsing","main":"split → trim → parse → collect; parse errors.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Split","Convert","Errors"],"captions":["\"1, 2, 3\".split(',') — three pieces, each with a stray space: trim","parse::<i32>() turns a piece into a number; we collect into a Vec<i32>","If a word is not a number, parse returns an error: unwrap stops the program, or we can skip or replace it"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"\"1\"","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"\" 2\"","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"\" 3\"","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let v: Vec<i32> = \"1, 2, 3\"","    .split(',')","    .map(|x| x.trim().parse().unwrap())","    .collect();"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"\"abc\".parse()\nErr","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"unwrap → panic\nunwrap_or(0)","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.4,21.6]}]},{"title":"Comparison and types","sub":"== and conversions","short":"Comparison","main":"== between String and &str; &s, as_str, to_string; parameters are &str.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["==","&str ↔ String","Function parameters"],"captions":["String and &str compare with ==; < and > go by bytes: capitals come before lowercase","&s or s.as_str() — String to &str; to_string(), String::from — back again","Functions should accept &str: a literal and a &String both fit; return String for new text"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["String::from(\"a\") == \"a\"   // true","\"Z\" < \"a\"                // true"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"String\n→ &s","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"&str\n→ to_string()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn shout(s: &str) -> String {","    s.to_uppercase()","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[15.1,32.3]}]},{"title":"Formatting","sub":"Width, precision","short":"Format","main":"{:>10}, {:.2}, {:?}, {name}.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Width and alignment","Precision and {:?}","Names"],"captions":["{:>10} — right, {:<10} — left, {:^10} — center; {:*^10} — with your own fill","{:.2} — two decimal places; {:?} — debug output; {:#?} — pretty multi-line","{name} right in the string, like f-strings; {0} and {x} — by number and by name"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["println!(\"[{:>6}]\", \"ab\");   // [    ab]","println!(\"[{:<6}]\", \"ab\");   // [ab    ]","println!(\"[{:^6}]\", \"ab\");   // [  ab  ]"],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["println!(\"{:.2}\", 3.14159);   // 3.14","println!(\"{:?}\", \"text\");     // \"text\"","println!(\"{:?}\", (1, 2));"],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let n = 5;","println!(\"{n} + {n} = {}\", n + n);"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[17.3,32.4]}]},{"title":"After Python","sub":"What changed","short":"After Python","main":"Two strings; len in bytes; format! instead of f-strings.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Two strings","Length and indexes","Methods"],"captions":["Python: one str; Rust: &str to read, String to own and change","Python: length and indexes by characters; Rust: len in bytes, characters via chars, no s[i]","f-strings → format!; strip → trim; join and split stay; + takes the left string"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"str","tone":"muted","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"&str / String","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"len → characters","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"len → bytes","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"f\"{x}\"","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"format!(\"{x}\")","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.9,26.9]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What next","short":"Summary","main":"Next: tuples, arrays, vectors.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Remember","Cheat sheet","Next"],"captions":["&str we read, String we own; length in bytes; characters via chars; slice at character boundaries","format! to concatenate; split, trim, parse to take text apart; {:>10} {:.2} {:?} for formatting","Next chapter: tuples, arrays and vectors"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"&str","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.